 " draws it."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"cd0fe90c-bb8d-464e-b97d-b95101896a75"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A shell is not a curve. On the square grid no two of its vertices are \
adjacent. The connected subsets of a shell that separate the centre from the \
outside form ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraSphere"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraSphere", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "e87d4b43-8890-452c-a32e-e3a3f75081a2"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"8e99dc00-0c44-4cdb-badd-1d94dc9ec628"],

Cell["\<\
A shell is all boundary, so its two measures part completely:\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b99f801c-a1b4-430a-be70-984a8f9ed369"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "f13781c7-b498-46ca-b39c-b2059dd805c4"], Cell["Measure", "TableText",
