  }]], "2ColumnTableMod",ExpressionUUID->"02bef475-8f3e-42af-ac88-\
b51dd8966ca0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "On the square grid, away from the rim, ",
 StyleBox["A(r) = 4r", "TI"],
 " for ",
 StyleBox["r \[GreaterEqual] 1", "TI"],
 "; on the cubic grid ",
 StyleBox["A(r) = 4r\.b2 + 2", "TI"],
 ". In general ",
 StyleBox["A(r)", "TI"],
 " is the difference of consecutive ball volumes. On a Riemannian manifold of \
dimension ",
 StyleBox["n", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["A(r) = n \[Omega]\:2099 r\:207f\:207b\.b9 (1 \[Minus] R r\.b2 / \
(6n) + O(r\:2074))", "TI"],
 ", with ",
 StyleBox["R", "TI"],
 " the scalar curvature at ",
 StyleBox["c", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"59d951e6-1c05-45af-9bfd-f79c09b3eb1c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Riemannian measure of a band drops its two rims. On the square grid, \
away from the rim, the band {",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 "} with ",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " \[GreaterEqual] 1 has the Riemannian measure of the counting measure of \
the band {",
 StyleBox["r", "TI"],
 " + 1, ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 " \[Minus] 1}."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"fb13f016-9f78-493a-b16b-505f4c66952d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A radius past the eccentricity of ",
 StyleBox["c", "TI"],
 " gives the empty shell."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e9b7c5e2-e81d-4a8a-87fa-7e315d169f51"],

